{"base_rate":0.4200792602377807,"brier":0.17204663143989435,"bss":0.2937697876821247,"bss_hi":0.3776285472408375,"bss_lo":0.18758598788123243,"chart":{"base":[606.7,61.3],"fp":[302.6,290.7],"lead":"62,239.3 272,216.6 482,176.5 692,105.6","note":{"base":"skill 0.29 — higher than 54% of cities","fp":"low end +10pp, high end +18pp","lead":"day-1 error 1.2 °C — better than 35% of cities","rel":"promised 2% → rained 13%; promised 94% → rained 77%"},"rel":"75.9,408.2 288.4,347.9 652.8,133.6"},"country":"SE","deep":false,"depth":["Rain-probability calibration","Calibration curve","Seasonal split"],"ece":0.1394319682959049,"ess":381.87327511865203,"html":{"answer":"\n<h2 id=\"answer\">The short answer for Umea</h2>\n<div class=\"verdict\">\n<p class=\"lead\"><b>The Umea rain forecast is moderately skilful, though 5 points on its probability scale are off by more than chance explains.</b></p>\n<p>When it says rain is <i>near certain</i> (99%), believe about\n<b>84%</b>. When it says rain is <i>very unlikely</i>\n(0%), there is still roughly a <b>10%</b> chance.</p>\n<p class=\"muted\">Based on 757 days, 2024-04-26 to\n2026-05-31. \"Rain\" means at least 0.2 mm measured at\nROBACKSDALEN, 2.3 km from the forecast grid point.\nSkill score 0.29, ranked 99 of\n213 &mdash; but see the rank <i>range</i>\n(66&ndash;152) before reading anything into\nthat position.</p>\n</div>\n\n<h3>What the percentages actually mean here</h3>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th class=\"num\">It said</th><th class=\"num\">It rained</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Days</th><th>Verdict</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td class='num'>0%</td><td class='num'><b>10%</b></td><td class='num'>223</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">underpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>8%</td><td class='num'><b>22%</b></td><td class='num'>76</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">underpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>23%</td><td class='num'><b>28%</b></td><td class='num'>78</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>49%</td><td class='num'><b>26%</b></td><td class='num'>72</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>78%</td><td class='num'><b>55%</b></td><td class='num'>71</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>99%</td><td class='num'><b>84%</b></td><td class='num'>237</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">5 of 6 groups are further from honest than chance\nalone can explain. The rest are indistinguishable from a perfect forecast.</p>\n","card":"\n<div class=\"gcard\">\n  <p class=\"gcard-head\"><b>Umea</b> <span class=\"muted\">Sweden</span></p>\n  <p class=\"gcard-tier\"><span class=\"tag ok\">Moderately skilful</span>\n    <span class=\"muted\">5 points off by more than chance</span></p>\n  <dl class=\"gcard-stats\">\n    <div><dt>Skill score</dt><dd>0.29</dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Rank</dt><dd>66&ndash;152\n      <span class=\"muted\">of 213</span></dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Record</dt><dd>757 <span class=\"muted\">days</span></dd></div>\n  </dl>\n  <p class=\"gcard-more\"><a href=\"#answer\">The full verdict for\n    Umea &darr;</a></p>\n</div>","curve":"\n<h2 id=\"curve\">The calibration curve</h2>\n<p>Each dot is a group of days sharing a similar forecast. Horizontal position\nis what was promised; vertical is what happened. <b>On the dashed diagonal =\nhonest.</b> Hover any dot for its sample size.</p>\n<figure><svg viewBox=\"0 0 430 430\" width=\"100%\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Calibration curve for Umea\"><rect class=\"chart-plot\" x=\"58\" y=\"18\" width=\"354\" height=\"364\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"58\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"382\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"58\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">0%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"386\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end